WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.033 --> 00:00:00.567
Our CNN

00:00:00.567 --> 00:00:01.701
political analyst, a New York Times

00:00:01.701 --> 00:00:03.536
senior political correspondent,

00:00:03.536 --> 00:00:04.237
and of course, Trump

00:00:04.237 --> 00:00:06.072
biographer Maggie Haberman is there

00:00:06.072 --> 00:00:08.074
and she joins us now by phone.

00:00:08.108 --> 00:00:08.942
Maggie, obviously,

00:00:08.942 --> 00:00:11.011
you heard the president's speech.

00:00:11.011 --> 00:00:12.445
We did not take it here live.

00:00:12.445 --> 00:00:14.481
What did you make of what he told

00:00:14.481 --> 00:00:15.215
his supporters

00:00:15.215 --> 00:00:16.249
compared to

00:00:16.249 --> 00:00:16.950
how he was acting

00:00:16.950 --> 00:00:18.084
when he was here in Florida

00:00:18.084 --> 00:00:19.586
earlier today?

00:00:19.886 --> 00:00:20.820
It's interesting, Kaitlan,

00:00:20.820 --> 00:00:21.521
there were two things

00:00:21.521 --> 00:00:23.123
that were striking about this speech.

00:00:23.123 --> 00:00:23.757
Number one

00:00:23.757 --> 00:00:25.091
is that he's going through,

00:00:25.091 --> 00:00:25.959
at least for part of it,

00:00:25.959 --> 00:00:27.761
a pretty dry recitation

00:00:27.761 --> 00:00:28.194
of what

00:00:28.194 --> 00:00:29.029
you're going to hear

00:00:29.029 --> 00:00:30.263
from him and his team,

00:00:30.263 --> 00:00:31.398
which is his claims

00:00:31.398 --> 00:00:32.165
and a misstatement

00:00:32.165 --> 00:00:34.034
of the Presidential Records Act,

00:00:34.034 --> 00:00:34.934
that he was entitled

00:00:34.934 --> 00:00:36.636
to keep these documents

00:00:36.636 --> 00:00:37.003
that, you know,

00:00:37.003 --> 00:00:38.438
no one else has been prosecuted

00:00:38.438 --> 00:00:39.973
for doing what he did.

00:00:39.973 --> 00:00:41.041
Prosecutors obviously

00:00:41.041 --> 00:00:42.142
say that he chose things

00:00:42.142 --> 00:00:43.243
that were among the nation's

00:00:43.243 --> 00:00:46.012
most important classified material.

00:00:46.012 --> 00:00:47.313
That's one thing that was striking.

00:00:47.313 --> 00:00:48.648
But the other that was striking

00:00:48.648 --> 00:00:50.483
is his delivery.

00:00:50.483 --> 00:00:52.886
He made such a show in Miami

00:00:53.019 --> 00:00:55.055
being seen at the restaurant for

00:00:55.055 --> 00:00:57.290
which is something of a landmark

00:00:58.191 --> 00:00:59.192
in Miami.

00:00:59.192 --> 00:01:00.727
And, you know,

00:01:00.727 --> 00:01:01.561
mingling with people

00:01:01.561 --> 00:01:02.729
and talking to people,

00:01:02.729 --> 00:01:05.465
very low energy tonight, very flat

00:01:05.465 --> 00:01:06.533
delivery and spent

00:01:06.533 --> 00:01:08.935
no time hanging out with the crowd

00:01:08.935 --> 00:01:10.804
or sort of basking in their glow

00:01:10.804 --> 00:01:11.371
afterwards,

00:01:11.371 --> 00:01:12.205
turned on appeal

00:01:12.205 --> 00:01:14.607
and walked back inside the Bedminster.

00:01:15.041 --> 00:01:16.042
And so I think

00:01:16.042 --> 00:01:17.210
this is going to be reality

00:01:17.210 --> 00:01:17.944
going forward.

00:01:17.944 --> 00:01:19.079
It's going to be him

00:01:19.079 --> 00:01:20.280
defending himself

00:01:20.280 --> 00:01:21.881
and offering up this claim

00:01:21.881 --> 00:01:22.615
that he had the right

00:01:22.615 --> 00:01:23.450
to do what he did,

00:01:23.450 --> 00:01:24.451
which, again, prosecutors

00:01:24.451 --> 00:01:25.919
say is not true.

00:01:25.919 --> 00:01:27.887
But it's mixed with real anger

00:01:27.887 --> 00:01:28.655
at the situation

00:01:31.791 --> 00:01:34.627
And Maggie, what does that say to you

00:01:34.627 --> 00:01:35.328
about giving

00:01:35.328 --> 00:01:35.595
I mean,

00:01:35.595 --> 00:01:36.062
you know, Trump

00:01:36.062 --> 00:01:37.864
better than almost anyone else,

00:01:37.864 --> 00:01:39.432
as you reported on him

00:01:39.432 --> 00:01:40.800
at length, any other reporter,

00:01:40.800 --> 00:01:41.634
I should note.

00:01:41.634 --> 00:01:42.535
What does it say to you

00:01:42.535 --> 00:01:43.837
about how he's actually viewing

00:01:43.837 --> 00:01:45.138
this privately compared

00:01:45.138 --> 00:01:47.040
to that bravado and bluster

00:01:47.040 --> 00:01:48.508
we saw at the restaurant?

00:01:48.508 --> 00:01:49.943
Here in Miami?

00:01:50.210 --> 00:01:51.111
What I hear,

00:01:51.111 --> 00:01:52.879
Caitlin, is it goes it goes up and down.

00:01:52.879 --> 00:01:54.013
But there are times where he is

00:01:54.013 --> 00:01:54.981
incredibly angry.

00:01:54.981 --> 00:01:56.649
I heard that he was really mad

00:01:56.649 --> 00:01:57.851
for the 90 minutes after that.

00:01:57.851 --> 00:01:59.819
He found out roughly around 7 p.m.

00:01:59.819 --> 00:02:00.787
on Thursday night

00:02:00.787 --> 00:02:01.955
that he had been indicted.

00:02:01.955 --> 00:02:03.089
And then he, you know,

00:02:03.089 --> 00:02:05.225
got it together, went to dinner with the.

00:02:05.825 --> 00:02:06.926
I thought he was very angry

00:02:06.926 --> 00:02:08.695
the next day when he saw the indictment.

00:02:08.695 --> 00:02:10.563
He was especially rattled

00:02:10.563 --> 00:02:13.366
by the photographs that were in the dark.

00:02:13.366 --> 00:02:14.300
In the indictment,

00:02:14.300 --> 00:02:16.136
he actually referenced the photographs,

00:02:16.136 --> 00:02:17.637
some of them anyway,

00:02:17.637 --> 00:02:19.772
from the stage tonight behind the podium.

00:02:20.340 --> 00:02:21.174
But then he has moments

00:02:21.174 --> 00:02:22.275
of almost ebullience.

00:02:22.275 --> 00:02:23.376
And, you know, it's

00:02:23.376 --> 00:02:25.378
hard for people around him to tell

00:02:25.378 --> 00:02:26.246
what's genuine

00:02:26.246 --> 00:02:26.946
versus him

00:02:26.946 --> 00:02:28.314
trying to keep up, as you said,

00:02:28.314 --> 00:02:30.316
that were part of more than the bravado.

00:02:30.316 --> 00:02:30.717
It's also

00:02:30.717 --> 00:02:32.652
just the facade that everything is fine

00:02:32.652 --> 00:02:34.687
because that's so much of how he how he

00:02:34.921 --> 00:02:36.656
stacking the books

00:02:38.424 --> 00:02:38.791
Yeah.

00:02:38.791 --> 00:02:40.093
Who did you see in the

00:02:40.093 --> 00:02:41.761
in the crowd tonight in Bedminster?

00:02:41.761 --> 00:02:44.030
Did anyone stand out to you?

00:02:44.264 --> 00:02:45.498
Well, many people stood out,

00:02:45.498 --> 00:02:46.232
but mostly

00:02:46.232 --> 00:02:47.634
because it was just such an eclectic

00:02:47.634 --> 00:02:50.970
group of people, said Gorka,

00:02:50.970 --> 00:02:52.739
who worked in the Trump White House

00:02:52.739 --> 00:02:54.941
and been one of the loudest defenders

00:02:55.508 --> 00:02:56.976
sort of on the on the fringe

00:02:56.976 --> 00:02:58.311
on the right.

00:02:58.311 --> 00:03:00.180
Ed Costa, chairman

00:03:00.180 --> 00:03:02.849
of the Republican Party.

00:03:04.217 --> 00:03:05.451
Bernie Kerik, the former

00:03:05.451 --> 00:03:07.187
NYPD commissioner

00:03:07.187 --> 00:03:08.855
A number of different people.

00:03:08.855 --> 00:03:11.691
Mike Lindell, the Mypillow CEO, you know,

00:03:12.759 --> 00:03:13.459
Tommy Tuberville,

00:03:13.459 --> 00:03:13.993
the senator

00:03:13.993 --> 00:03:15.395
who is supposed to be there tonight.

00:03:15.395 --> 00:03:16.829
But for the most part, Caitlyn

00:03:16.829 --> 00:03:18.264
you know, these were the diehards.

00:03:18.264 --> 00:03:19.866
These were people who

00:03:19.866 --> 00:03:20.533
were asked

00:03:20.533 --> 00:03:22.669
by Trump's staff to be here or,

00:03:22.669 --> 00:03:24.270
you know, who loved the chance

00:03:24.270 --> 00:03:26.072
to see the former president.

00:03:26.072 --> 00:03:26.873
But there were not

00:03:26.873 --> 00:03:27.273
names of

00:03:27.273 --> 00:03:29.342
people who were in his administration

00:03:29.342 --> 00:03:30.410
or even on his past

00:03:30.410 --> 00:03:31.411
presidential campaign.

00:03:31.411 --> 00:03:32.545
So you're looking at a very,

00:03:32.545 --> 00:03:34.214
very different chief here.

00:03:36.983 --> 00:03:37.350
Yeah.

00:03:37.350 --> 00:03:38.551
And of course, it's telling

00:03:38.551 --> 00:03:40.220
who he surrounds himself with.

00:03:40.220 --> 00:03:40.620
Maggie,

00:03:40.620 --> 00:03:41.387
you say it's clear

00:03:41.387 --> 00:03:42.021
that he's determined

00:03:42.021 --> 00:03:42.956
to fight these charges,

00:03:42.956 --> 00:03:45.225
obviously in the court of public opinion.

00:03:45.458 --> 00:03:46.092
A lot of questions

00:03:46.092 --> 00:03:47.026
on what his legal strategy

00:03:47.026 --> 00:03:49.262
actually in the courthouse looks like.

00:03:49.462 --> 00:03:50.730
Does this remind you

00:03:50.730 --> 00:03:51.397
in any way

00:03:51.397 --> 00:03:52.465
of how he responded

00:03:52.465 --> 00:03:54.000
to what is obviously

00:03:54.000 --> 00:03:55.702
a very different situation

00:03:55.702 --> 00:03:57.804
but also came with a lot of fallout,

00:03:57.804 --> 00:03:58.905
which was the Access

00:03:58.905 --> 00:04:00.106
Hollywood tape

00:04:00.106 --> 00:04:00.773
that came around,

00:04:00.773 --> 00:04:01.541
of course, the last time

00:04:01.541 --> 00:04:03.443
he was running for president?

00:04:03.443 --> 00:04:04.310
Very much so.

00:04:04.310 --> 00:04:05.912
He has basically you know,

00:04:05.912 --> 00:04:07.113
a few moves, Caitlyn,

00:04:07.113 --> 00:04:08.848
that he does over and over again.

00:04:08.848 --> 00:04:11.050
And we saw it for the first time

00:04:11.050 --> 00:04:12.218
in his political life

00:04:12.218 --> 00:04:14.320
when the Access Hollywood tape came out.

00:04:14.621 --> 00:04:15.588
His impulse

00:04:15.588 --> 00:04:17.357
you know, again,

00:04:17.357 --> 00:04:19.492
was when a crowd of his supporters

00:04:19.492 --> 00:04:20.960
had a mass on Fifth Avenue

00:04:20.960 --> 00:04:22.328
in front of the Trump Tower

00:04:22.328 --> 00:04:23.396
was to go down

00:04:23.396 --> 00:04:23.997
and literally

00:04:23.997 --> 00:04:25.331
immersed himself in the crowd.

00:04:25.331 --> 00:04:26.199
I was there for

00:04:26.199 --> 00:04:28.501
it was a really striking image.

00:04:28.501 --> 00:04:29.302
And it was almost as if

00:04:29.302 --> 00:04:31.170
he was giving himself a pep talk,

00:04:31.170 --> 00:04:31.437
you know,

00:04:31.437 --> 00:04:32.639
clapping his hands together

00:04:32.639 --> 00:04:33.773
and getting himself

00:04:33.773 --> 00:04:34.440
locked up

00:04:34.440 --> 00:04:35.775
a bit of what we saw

00:04:35.775 --> 00:04:37.443
similarly in Miami today,

00:04:37.443 --> 00:04:38.411
that is the impulse

00:04:38.411 --> 00:04:39.078
is to just sort of

00:04:39.078 --> 00:04:40.713
immerse myself in the crowd.

00:04:40.713 --> 00:04:41.914
But that's not what we saw

00:04:41.914 --> 00:04:42.849
in the speech tonight.

00:04:42.849 --> 00:04:43.149
Again,

00:04:43.149 --> 00:04:45.785
this was a carefully written speech

00:04:45.785 --> 00:04:46.919
by some of his advisers

00:04:46.919 --> 00:04:48.454
because he's laying out

00:04:48.454 --> 00:04:49.022
what what

00:04:49.022 --> 00:04:50.556
resembles a legal argument,

00:04:50.556 --> 00:04:51.357
but which is really about

00:04:51.357 --> 00:04:52.925
the court of public opinion.

00:04:52.925 --> 00:04:53.960
But he was

00:04:53.960 --> 00:04:55.828
he was deflated as he was getting it

00:04:55.828 --> 00:04:56.829
or seemed deflated.

00:04:56.829 --> 00:04:58.064
But I do think, yes,

00:04:58.064 --> 00:04:59.065
this as Bill

00:04:59.065 --> 00:05:00.700
echoes his immediate reaction

00:05:00.700 --> 00:05:02.201
on all of these moments,

00:05:02.201 --> 00:05:04.170
is to surround himself

00:05:04.170 --> 00:05:05.305
with his supporters

00:05:05.305 --> 00:05:06.406
and beat them

00:05:06.406 --> 00:05:08.541
both as a bully for his emotions

00:05:08.541 --> 00:05:10.310
and also as a shield against what says

00:05:13.179 --> 00:05:13.613
another

00:05:13.613 --> 00:05:15.415
person he's surrounding himself with

00:05:15.415 --> 00:05:16.716
is his codefendant.

00:05:16.716 --> 00:05:17.917
Well, not

00:05:17.984 --> 00:05:18.584
just moments

00:05:18.584 --> 00:05:19.285
after they left

00:05:19.285 --> 00:05:21.087
the courthouse here behind me today,

00:05:21.087 --> 00:05:22.588
they were seen together

00:05:22.588 --> 00:05:23.256
at that restaurant.

00:05:23.256 --> 00:05:24.657
Obviously, the judge has said

00:05:24.657 --> 00:05:25.291
they are not supposed

00:05:25.291 --> 00:05:26.759
to discuss this case

00:05:26.759 --> 00:05:28.761
except through attorneys.

00:05:28.761 --> 00:05:29.729
Do you think that that is

00:05:29.729 --> 00:05:30.730
actually something

00:05:30.730 --> 00:05:33.733
that the president will abide by?

00:05:33.733 --> 00:05:35.001
Caitlin, I think that, you know,

00:05:35.001 --> 00:05:37.770
the former president as well as I do.

00:05:37.770 --> 00:05:38.504
And I think that,

00:05:38.504 --> 00:05:40.440
you know, that not being told

00:05:40.440 --> 00:05:41.841
not to do something as often

00:05:41.841 --> 00:05:43.576
and as it is for him to do something,

00:05:43.576 --> 00:05:45.812
especially this by a person in authority.

00:05:45.812 --> 00:05:46.746
So I think this is going to be

00:05:46.746 --> 00:05:48.047
a real challenge.

00:05:48.047 --> 00:05:48.948
You know, it is

00:05:48.948 --> 00:05:50.516
it is invariably,

00:05:50.516 --> 00:05:51.184
if they're talking

00:05:51.184 --> 00:05:52.952
I suspect, going to be worked so

00:05:52.952 --> 00:05:53.553
well now that

00:05:53.553 --> 00:05:55.121
because he is the codefendant,

00:05:55.121 --> 00:05:56.923
not a former president,

00:05:56.923 --> 00:05:58.691
and he has a very different circumstance,

00:05:58.691 --> 00:06:00.626
he also has not been arraigned

00:06:00.626 --> 00:06:02.195
because he did not have local counsel.

00:06:02.195 --> 00:06:03.963
He still has to go back to court

00:06:03.963 --> 00:06:05.131
in two weeks.

00:06:05.131 --> 00:06:06.232
But I think that, you know,

00:06:06.232 --> 00:06:08.067
not talking about the case

00:06:08.067 --> 00:06:09.268
with either Wolf now

00:06:09.268 --> 00:06:10.036
or witnesses

00:06:10.036 --> 00:06:11.170
or the government is expected

00:06:11.170 --> 00:06:13.072
to produce a list to say

00:06:13.072 --> 00:06:13.773
these are people Trump

00:06:13.773 --> 00:06:15.375
should not be talking directly to,

00:06:15.375 --> 00:06:17.577
only to a counsel related to the case.

00:06:17.577 --> 00:06:18.144
It's going to be it's

00:06:18.144 --> 00:06:20.546
going to be a Herculean task to get

00:06:20.546 --> 00:06:20.947
an option

00:06:24.083 --> 00:06:24.350
Yeah.

00:06:24.350 --> 00:06:25.385
We'll see what that looks like.

00:06:25.385 --> 00:06:27.320
Maggie Haberman from Bedminster

00:06:27.320 --> 00:06:28.321
in New Jersey at the former

00:06:28.321 --> 00:06:29.922
Presidents Club, thank you.

00:06:29.922 --> 00:06:30.356
Joining us

00:06:30.356 --> 00:06:32.325
now here in Miami, David Weinstein

00:06:32.325 --> 00:06:33.526
a former assistant U.S.

00:06:33.526 --> 00:06:34.227
attorney

00:06:34.227 --> 00:06:35.762
from the Southern District of Florida

00:06:35.762 --> 00:06:36.529
and also

00:06:36.529 --> 00:06:38.164
former chief of public integrity

00:06:38.164 --> 00:06:39.465
in the Justice Department

00:06:39.465 --> 00:06:40.500
South Florida office.

00:06:40.500 --> 00:06:41.300
One of the perfect people

00:06:41.300 --> 00:06:43.403
to talk about all of this with.

00:06:43.403 --> 00:06:44.036
We'll get back to

00:06:44.036 --> 00:06:44.904
what the former president

00:06:44.904 --> 00:06:46.305
is saying tonight in just a moment.

00:06:46.305 --> 00:06:47.640
But what you saw today

00:06:47.640 --> 00:06:49.475
happening in this courthouse behind us.

00:06:49.475 --> 00:06:50.910
Do you believe that's the way

00:06:50.910 --> 00:06:52.245
that anyone else would be treated?

00:06:52.245 --> 00:06:53.646
Do you think he was treated differently?

00:06:53.646 --> 00:06:54.981
Not for a second.

00:06:54.981 --> 00:06:56.883
He was given special treatment,

00:06:56.883 --> 00:06:57.617
the likes of which

00:06:57.617 --> 00:06:58.951
I've never seen before.

00:06:58.951 --> 00:07:00.286
Any other defendant charged

00:07:00.286 --> 00:07:01.821
with that many violations.

00:07:01.821 --> 00:07:03.790
Possessing that many top secret

00:07:03.790 --> 00:07:05.458
classified documents,

00:07:05.458 --> 00:07:06.092
then charged

00:07:06.092 --> 00:07:06.926
with obstructing

00:07:06.926 --> 00:07:08.928
justice, making false statements

00:07:08.928 --> 00:07:10.830
and having another open

00:07:10.830 --> 00:07:13.065
pending felony case

00:07:13.065 --> 00:07:13.800
would have been hard

00:07:13.800 --> 00:07:15.001
pressed for the government

00:07:15.001 --> 00:07:16.636
not to ask for detention

00:07:16.636 --> 00:07:18.471
and for that defendant

00:07:18.471 --> 00:07:19.872
to be sitting behind bars

00:07:19.872 --> 00:07:20.640
waiting to see

00:07:20.640 --> 00:07:21.841
whether or not he'd get out.

00:07:21.841 --> 00:07:24.143
This defendant was released

00:07:24.143 --> 00:07:25.511
under virtually no conditions.

00:07:25.511 --> 00:07:26.546
So you believe,

00:07:26.546 --> 00:07:27.447
even though

00:07:27.447 --> 00:07:28.614
the way the former president

00:07:28.614 --> 00:07:29.682
and his legal team framed it,

00:07:29.682 --> 00:07:30.483
which is that

00:07:30.483 --> 00:07:32.051
they're being treated unfairly by

00:07:32.051 --> 00:07:34.053
by the prosecution, by the courts here,

00:07:34.053 --> 00:07:35.154
they're actually going out of their way

00:07:35.154 --> 00:07:36.155
to accommodate him.

00:07:36.155 --> 00:07:37.723
Absolutely. Bending over backwards.

00:07:37.723 --> 00:07:39.425
The fact that he didn't get arrested

00:07:39.425 --> 00:07:40.693
Friday morning,

00:07:40.693 --> 00:07:43.229
where he was living in the dark hours

00:07:43.229 --> 00:07:45.431
and brought before a magistrate judge

00:07:45.431 --> 00:07:46.732
to make his initial appearance

00:07:46.732 --> 00:07:48.034
on a sealed indictment.

00:07:48.034 --> 00:07:50.303
That's what happens in the normal case.

00:07:50.303 --> 00:07:51.270
So when you hear

00:07:51.270 --> 00:07:52.038
what the former president

00:07:52.038 --> 00:07:52.772
was saying tonight,

00:07:52.772 --> 00:07:54.974
talking about the Espionage Act

00:07:54.974 --> 00:07:55.975
and how that is

00:07:55.975 --> 00:07:58.044
part of the charges that have been

00:07:58.277 --> 00:07:59.779
that are part of this indictment,

00:07:59.779 --> 00:08:00.913
he was had this quote

00:08:00.913 --> 00:08:01.514
that was saying

00:08:01.514 --> 00:08:03.716
that it's used for spies, for traitors.

00:08:03.716 --> 00:08:04.684
But it's obviously

00:08:04.684 --> 00:08:06.519
much more expansive than that.

00:08:06.519 --> 00:08:08.688
What he's saying about it is incorrect.

00:08:08.855 --> 00:08:10.056
Absolutely incorrect.

00:08:10.056 --> 00:08:10.656
Look, it's

00:08:10.656 --> 00:08:11.491
part of a larger

00:08:11.491 --> 00:08:12.692
act, the Espionage Act,

00:08:12.692 --> 00:08:15.695
and it covers people who had at one time

00:08:15.695 --> 00:08:17.330
access to documents

00:08:17.330 --> 00:08:18.297
because they had clearance

00:08:18.297 --> 00:08:19.465
to have those documents.

00:08:19.465 --> 00:08:21.133
And then they took those documents

00:08:21.133 --> 00:08:21.701
from a place

00:08:21.701 --> 00:08:23.169
where they should have been

00:08:23.169 --> 00:08:25.004
under secure quarters

00:08:25.004 --> 00:08:26.105
and either held them or

00:08:26.105 --> 00:08:27.373
kept them somewhere else

00:08:27.373 --> 00:08:29.108
or share them with other people.

00:08:29.108 --> 00:08:29.709
That's what

00:08:29.709 --> 00:08:31.911
it is alleged that he has done.

00:08:32.178 --> 00:08:34.213
It doesn't have to be a mail drop

00:08:34.213 --> 00:08:35.882
where spy versus spy

00:08:35.882 --> 00:08:37.350
meet each other somewhere

00:08:37.350 --> 00:08:39.352
and hand over secret documents.

00:08:39.352 --> 00:08:40.686
It's the improper

00:08:40.686 --> 00:08:42.722
use and handling of classified documents.

00:08:42.722 --> 00:08:44.490
And in this case, documents

00:08:44.490 --> 00:08:45.124
that were alleged

00:08:45.124 --> 00:08:46.459
to contain defense

00:08:46.459 --> 00:08:48.394
and military secrets of our country

00:08:48.394 --> 00:08:50.463
and that were stored in places

00:08:50.463 --> 00:08:52.398
you know, he's there at the former club

00:08:52.398 --> 00:08:53.366
or at his club tonight,

00:08:53.366 --> 00:08:54.433
where we also know

00:08:54.433 --> 00:08:56.135
he took boxes of documents up

00:08:56.135 --> 00:08:57.603
to Bedminster with him

00:08:57.603 --> 00:08:58.337
when it comes to

00:08:58.337 --> 00:08:59.138
what's next

00:08:59.138 --> 00:09:00.740
and what a trial looks like here.

00:09:00.740 --> 00:09:02.608
How fast do you think we could see

00:09:02.608 --> 00:09:04.544
a trial potentially in this case?

00:09:04.544 --> 00:09:06.279
It's not going to occur that quickly

00:09:06.279 --> 00:09:08.281
in a regular case.

00:09:08.281 --> 00:09:09.148
They move fast

00:09:09.148 --> 00:09:10.082
here in the southern district.

00:09:10.082 --> 00:09:10.883
Of Florida,

00:09:10.883 --> 00:09:13.085
trial be set in a couple of months.

00:09:13.085 --> 00:09:13.553
It'll be

00:09:13.553 --> 00:09:15.721
perhaps continued a little bit, case

00:09:15.721 --> 00:09:17.490
to be resolved in six to nine months.

00:09:17.490 --> 00:09:19.191
But here you have security

00:09:19.191 --> 00:09:21.427
clearances are needed for his counsel.

00:09:21.627 --> 00:09:23.429
You're going to have motion practice.

00:09:23.429 --> 00:09:24.330
You're going to have motions,

00:09:24.330 --> 00:09:25.798
and undoubtedly you're going to end up

00:09:25.798 --> 00:09:26.966
at the 11th Circuit

00:09:26.966 --> 00:09:28.100
and requests

00:09:28.100 --> 00:09:28.901
for continuance

00:09:28.901 --> 00:09:30.870
to try and push this matter off

00:09:30.870 --> 00:09:32.405
past the November election.

00:09:32.405 --> 00:09:33.573
So in a case

00:09:33.573 --> 00:09:34.807
that could normally be resolved

00:09:34.807 --> 00:09:36.542
by March or April.

00:09:36.542 --> 00:09:37.677
This one's going to drag out

00:09:37.677 --> 00:09:39.145
at least until the summer.

00:09:39.145 --> 00:09:40.413
Well, and of course, the question is,

00:09:40.413 --> 00:09:41.113
does it happen

00:09:41.113 --> 00:09:43.082
before the 20, 24 election?

00:09:43.082 --> 00:09:44.850
We'll wait to see David Weinstein.

00:09:44.850 --> 00:09:45.184
Of course,

00:09:45.184 --> 00:09:46.118
you are the perfect person

00:09:46.118 --> 00:09:46.786
to talk about this.

00:09:46.786 --> 00:09:47.019
You've been

00:09:47.019 --> 00:09:48.254
in that courthouse many times.

00:09:48.254 --> 00:09:49.422
Thank you for joining us today.

00:09:49.422 --> 00:09:49.922
You're welcome.

